# DIAGNOSTICS

Every message is in the log; `compile` fails when the log has an error, `link` throws when its has one.

# BUGS

A cube sampler's SPIR-V is made, but the layer's lowering refuses a cube image, so a program that samples one (`textureCube`) does not reach the device.
The core and the Valhall backend have no texture access in a vertex stage, so a vertex shader that samples (glmark2's terrain) is linked and lowered and then refused.
The Valhall backend accepts gl_PointSize and does not store it.
Appendix A's restrictions on loops and indices are not enforced: more programs compile than GL ES 2.0 promises.
`invariant` decorates the outputs, which the compiler keeps as written; nothing more is done for it.
The varyings' packing is estimated (a vec3's spare column taking a float, two vec2s sharing a row), not packed as appendix A.7's algorithm does, and each vector takes a location of its own.
A sampler array indexed by a value is sampled one element at a time, so it costs as many lookups as the array is long.
